            <ArticleTitle>In search of the 'back mouse'.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>657-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The &quot;back mouse&quot; is a tender, fibrous, fatty subcutaneous nodule found in the lumbosacral area in up to 16% of people. It can be a treatable cause of low back pain that may be unrecognized by both specialists and generalists.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
